cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below. State which file and which date you used."
type: dataset
title: "Dental AI Visibility Data: US Dental Practice Websites, AI Search Crawler Access, and a Vendor Self-Measurement Run Log (2026)"
abstract: >-
  Five anonymized, aggregated CSV datasets. Four are dental market scans covering
  how US dental practice websites are built and how they respond to AI search
  crawlers: structured data, publishing platform, robots.txt handling of 13 named
  AI and data crawlers, live server behavior toward those crawlers, Google review
  and rating signals, and site speed. They are built from Citevio's own scans of
  527 dental practices (7 US metros plus 9 smaller nearby towns, June 2026),
  6,497 dental-related domains nationwide (July 2026), and 499 sites tested for
  live crawler access (July 2026). The fifth file is a separately marked vendor
  self-measurement log: 13 completed answer-engine runs (August 2026) recording
  whether the publisher's own name and domain appeared in responses to fixed
  queries. It measures the publisher, not the market, and supports no statement
  about dental practices. Row-level records, practice domains, and raw engine
  response text are not published; every file holds counts or per-run outcome
  flags only.
